  "metric": {
    "description": "Geometric mean of three independently reported components.\n`project_run_layout_f1` is an F1 over (bioproject, run_accession, library_layout) triples, so filing a run under the wrong project costs the same as missing it.\n`metadata_f1` is an F1 over (run_accession, field, normalized_value) triples restricted to the fifteen stable fields listed below and stated in the query.\n`exact_run_content_f1` is an F1 over runs, not over reads. Each expected run is one binary unit: its whole (sequence, quality) multiset must match the stored fingerprint, and there is no partial credit inside a run. The name says so deliberately - an earlier draft described this as read-level F1, which it is not. A run only half retrieved is a failed retrieval, not a differently shaped scientific answer, and a truncated run therefore costs exactly what a wholly wrong one does.\n",
    "type": "retrieval_composite"
  },
  "reference_accuracy": 1.0
